=== PART 3 -- THE PRESCRIBED CHECK, STATED FORMALLY AND DECIDED ===
  PRESCRIBED: "a table's `N frames` is the product of the free bits it describes".
  A free bit is a binary choice, so a product of free bits is a POWER OF TWO,
  and the check is  N = 2^f  for the f free bits of THE enumeration.
  table                             N factorisation    2-power?   verdict
  (Z3) z_0 & z_0                  832 2*2*2*2*2*2*13   NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 13)
  (Z4) z_0 & z_1                  832 2*2*2*2*2*2*13   NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 13)
  (Z4) z_0 & z_2                  858 2*3*11*13        NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 13)
  (Z4) z_0 & z_3                  872 2*2*2*109        NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 109)
  (Z4) z_0 & z_4                  858 2*3*11*13        NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 13)
  (Z4) z_0 & z_5                  832 2*2*2*2*2*2*13   NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 13)
  (Z5) one slot                    32 2*2*2*2*2        yes        PASSES BY ACCIDENT (no branch has 5 free bits)
  (Z5) two slots                  768 2*2*2*2*2*2*2*2*3 NO         CANNOT PASS (odd prime factor 3)
  [PASS] the prescribed check CANNOT be passed by SEVEN of the eight tables, because their populations carry odd prime factors and a free-bit product cannot  -- 7 tables cannot pass
  [PASS] and of the two tables that CAN pass, at least one passes for a FALSE reason (no branch has that many free bits)  -- 1 accidental passes

  SO: the check is not 'failed', it is ILL-POSED.  There is no 'the free bits
  it describes' -- each table is a SUM over branches with DIFFERENT free-bit
  counts.  The satisfiable form of the check is
        N  =  SUM over branches of ( 2^{f_b} - degenerate )
  which needs the branch list, and the branch list is not in the brief.

